  "caption": "Deadline day: Quinn forgot to breathe, the shoulders crept up, and by 4pm the neck felt like concrete.\n\nBreathing high into the upper chest all day can keep extra work on the neck muscles. Breathing retraining can be a useful part of care for some neck pain, but it won't reshape your ribs or replace strength training.\n\nWhat often helps: breathe low and slow through the nose, letting the ribs widen sideways; take a few slow breaths during desk breaks; learn to brace properly for heavy lifts; and keep active treatment and strength work going.\n\nBreathlessness, chest tightness or dizziness should be checked by your GP first. Snoring or daytime sleepiness is worth a GP chat too.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
